+/// A global lock that serializes the addition of epoll-to-epoll interest entries.
+///
+/// Without it, two threads adding an epoll file `A` into `B` and `B` into `A` could both observe an
+/// acyclic interest graph and both proceed, building a cycle that neither of them saw. The lock is
+/// only taken when the file being added is itself an epoll file, so ordinary files never contend on
+/// it.
+///
+/// Reference: <https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.17/source/fs/eventpoll.c#L61-L68>.
+static EPOLL_NESTED_ADD_LOCK: Mutex<()> = Mutex::new(());
